# Example env for HyAtlas v4 — pure Go.
# Set these in the shell or service unit that starts hyatlas-go.
# Every variable below is read by the server (grep the .go files for HYATLAS_).

# LLM (fact extraction, summary, intention, and ultra consolidation)
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint works — Nous Portal, a local ollama/vLLM/
# llama.cpp server, or anything else. The model id is whatever that endpoint
# serves; a Nous Portal :free id is only one option among many.
# No endpoint is assumed by the server. Extraction sends memory text to whatever
# you set here, so it is your choice. Leave these unset and writes store the raw
# trace only, with llm=unconfigured in status (or run HYATLAS_MODE=lite for no LLM
# call at all). The endpoint, model and key must all be set for an LLM call.
#
# The values below are a free Nous Portal endpoint, offered as a starting point
# by the installer (scripts/install.sh) -- uncomment to use it. `hermes memory
# setup` has no default endpoint; enter any OpenAI-compatible URL there.
#HYATLAS_LLM_BASE=https://inference-api.nousresearch.com/v1
#HYATLAS_LLM_MODEL=poolside/laguna-s-2.1:free
#HYATLAS_LLM_KEY=YOUR_KEY_HERE
# Optional: read the key live from a file on every call instead of freezing it
# at startup — for rotating credentials (e.g. the 1-hour JWT Hermes keeps fresh
# in its auth.json). Accepts that auth.json shape (providers.nous.agent_key, or
# access_token) or a plain-text file holding the bare token. When set, it wins
# over HYATLAS_LLM_KEY, which is the fallback if the file cannot be read.
#HYATLAS_LLM_KEY_FILE=/path/to/auth.json

# Embeddings — in-process BGE-small by default; no env vars needed.
#HYATLAS_EMBED_BASE=bge       # default. Local, no network.
#HYATLAS_EMBED_BASE=local     # offline deterministic stub, for tests only (not semantic)
#HYATLAS_EMBED_BASE=https://...   # any OpenAI-compatible embeddings URL. Every write
#                              and every search query text is then sent there, in
#                              every mode, including lite.
#HYATLAS_EMBED_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small   # used only when EMBED_BASE is a URL
#HYATLAS_EMBED_KEY=YOUR_EMBED_KEY            # bearer token for that URL, if it needs one

# Model directory for a plain (non-embedded) build. A release binary is embedded
# and ignores this. When set, it is the ONLY directory searched. When unset, the
# server looks in <cwd>/models, then <exe dir>/models, then ~/.hyatlas/models
# (Windows: %LOCALAPPDATA%\hyatlas\models).
#HYATLAS_MODEL_DIR=/path/to/models

# Port and bind address. Loopback only by default.
HYATLAS_GO_PORT=19528
#HYATLAS_GO_HOST=127.0.0.1
# IPv6 literals work with or without brackets (::1 or [::1]).
# The server has no authentication. Do not bind it to a network interface you do
# not trust.

# Host allowlist. A request whose Host names a DNS name is refused with 403 unless
# that name is listed here. This applies to every route, /healthz included, and on
# every bind address. Localhost and IP literals always pass. Entries are hostnames
# only (no scheme, no port; a port in an entry is ignored). Comma-separated.
# Set this when you reach the server by a name, such as a LAN hostname behind a
# reverse proxy. Leave it unset otherwise, since that blocks DNS rebinding.
#HYATLAS_ALLOWED_HOSTS=memory.example.internal

# Data directory: chromem collections, doc_index.json, consolidate_state.json and
# the graph. Relative paths resolve against the working directory.
# Default: ./data
#HYATLAS_GO_DATA=/var/lib/hyatlas
# Graph store location. Default: <data>/graph.json
#HYATLAS_GRAPH_PATH=/var/lib/hyatlas/graph.json

# Extraction mode — a ladder of reasoning scope, not of latency:
#   lite   no LLM call, so no text goes to an LLM. With the default local
#          embeddings nothing leaves the machine (1/7 layers: L2)
#   pro    one extraction per write; reasons within that single turn
#          (5/7 layers: L1, L2, L3, L4, L7 — System1)
#   ultra  pro plus the slow path: periodic consolidation across memories,
#          which adds L5 knowledge and L6 schemas (7/7 layers at steady state;
#          HYATLAS_CONSOLIDATE_GRAPH=off drops L5, leaving 6/7)
# Default when unset: ultra. An unrecognised value is fatal at startup.
HYATLAS_MODE=ultra

# Whether a write BLOCKS on extraction (separate from the mode above).
# Unset follows the mode: pro blocks, ultra returns immediately ("pending").
# A server the Hermes plugin spawns defaults to off.
#HYATLAS_SYNC_EXTRACT=off

# Ultra only — slow-path tuning. Durations are Go durations (30m, 6h, 2160h) or a
# plain number of seconds. "d" is not a Go unit, so write days as hours.
# The interval must be positive in ultra; use HYATLAS_MODE=pro to skip the pass.
#HYATLAS_CONSOLIDATE_EVERY=6h       # default 6h
# Max facts per owner per consolidation call. An owner with more facts than this
# is consolidated in successive windows across passes. Default 50.
#HYATLAS_CONSOLIDATE_BATCH=50
# Age after which an L2 Raw memory is deleted, unless a live graph edge or a live
# fact still cites it. Unset (the default) means raw history is never deleted.
# 2160h is 90 days. An invalid value is logged and treated as unset.
#HYATLAS_RAW_RETENTION=2160h
